Deploy a fine-tuned model to Azure Cognitive Services

Usage
  azd ai finetuning jobs deploy [flags]

Flags
  -c, --capacity int32         : Capacity units (default 1)
  -d, --deployment-name string : Deployment name (required)
  -i, --job-id string          : Fine-tuning job ID (required)
  -m, --model-format string    : Model format (default "OpenAI")
      --no-wait                : Do not wait for deployment to complete
  -k, --sku string             : SKU for deployment (default "GlobalStandard")
  -v, --version string         : Model version (default "1")

Global Flags
      --debug                   : Enable debug mode
  -h, --help                    : help for deploy
      --no-prompt               : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
      --project-endpoint string : Azure AI Foundry project endpoint URL (e.g., https://account.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/project-name)
  -s, --subscription string     : Azure subscription ID (enables implicit init if environment not configured)

Examples
  Deploy the model produced by a fine-tuning job
    azd ai finetuning jobs deploy --job-id <job-id> --deployment-name my-model
